1. DEFINITIONS

"Licensor" means the owner or authorized controller of the Software and the
associated intellectual property rights.

"Tec-Tac Core" means the Tec-Tac server-side framework, runtime, APIs,
contracts, installers, supporting scripts, and related proprietary components.

"Tec-Tac UI" means the Tec-Tac user interface, shell, frontend framework,
styles, assets, and related proprietary components.

"Module" means an independently developed extension, integration, connector,
reportset, script package, or other add-on that interacts with Tec-Tac through
documented and supported public APIs, contracts, capabilities, or extension
points.

"Documentation" means documentation supplied by the Licensor for the Software.

"Licensee" means the person or entity lawfully licensed to use the Software.

2. PROPRIETARY SOFTWARE

Tec-Tac Core and Tec-Tac UI are proprietary commercial software. Except for the
limited rights expressly granted by this Agreement, all rights, title, and
interest in and to the Software, including all copyright, source code, object
code, architecture, designs, interfaces, documentation, and other intellectual
property, are reserved by the Licensor.

No rights are granted by implication, estoppel, or otherwise.

3. LICENSE GRANT

Subject to payment of all applicable fees, compliance with this Agreement, and
any applicable license certificate, entitlement, subscription, or order, the
Licensor grants the Licensee a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
non-sublicensable right to install and use the Software on the number of servers,
instances, users, devices, or other licensed units for which valid entitlement
has been granted.

Where the applicable license permits managed-service-provider use, the Licensee
may use the Software in providing technology or managed services to its own
customers, provided that the Licensee does not provide, sublicense, resell, or
make Tec-Tac itself available as a standalone hosted platform or software
product except under a separate written agreement.

4. TEC-TAC CORE AND TEC-TAC UI MAY NOT BE MODIFIED

The Licensee must not, and must not permit any third party to:

(a) modify, alter, adapt, patch, translate, or create derivative works from
    Tec-Tac Core or Tec-Tac UI;
(b) replace, monkey-patch, inject into, override, or otherwise alter proprietary
    Tec-Tac Core or Tec-Tac UI implementation code except through an expressly
    documented and supported extension mechanism;
(c) reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, decode, or otherwise attempt to
    derive source code, internal implementation details, or non-public interfaces
    from distributed object code, except only to the limited extent that such a
    restriction is prohibited by applicable law;
(d) remove, obscure, or alter copyright, trademark, proprietary, attribution,
    licensing, or entitlement notices;
(e) bypass, disable, circumvent, interfere with, or tamper with license,
    entitlement, access-control, security, integrity, or usage-enforcement
    mechanisms;
(f) distribute, publish, disclose, sublicense, rent, lease, lend, sell, resell,
    transfer, or otherwise make Tec-Tac Core or Tec-Tac UI available to another
    party except as expressly authorized in writing by the Licensor; or
(g) use proprietary Tec-Tac Core or Tec-Tac UI source code to create or assist
    in creating a competing or substitute platform.

5. MODULE AND EXTENSION DEVELOPMENT

The Licensee and third-party developers may develop independent Modules for the
Tec-Tac ecosystem.

Modules may interact with Tec-Tac only through documented and supported public
APIs, contracts, capabilities, module interfaces, scheduler interfaces,
registration mechanisms, or other extension points expressly made available for
that purpose.

Permission to develop Modules does not grant permission to modify Tec-Tac Core
or Tec-Tac UI, to depend on undocumented private implementation details, to
write directly to proprietary Core data structures where no public contract is
provided, or to bypass any security, licensing, RBAC, lifecycle, or integrity
control.

A Module independently developed without incorporating proprietary Tec-Tac Core
or Tec-Tac UI source code remains the intellectual property of its respective
developer, subject to any separate agreement applicable to that Module.

The Licensor does not claim ownership of independently developed Modules merely
because they use documented Tec-Tac extension interfaces.

The Licensor is not required to preserve undocumented or unsupported internal
interfaces and does not guarantee compatibility for Modules that rely on them.

6. LICENSED FEATURES, MODULES, AND ENTITLEMENTS

The Software may enforce licensing at server, instance, module, feature, user,
device, or other entitlement levels.

Possession of Software files does not itself grant an entitlement to use every
feature or Module. Features or Modules for which no valid entitlement exists may
be unavailable, disabled, restricted, or placed into a read-only state.

The Licensee must not share, duplicate, forge, manipulate, or circumvent license
keys, server identities, entitlement records, signatures, activation data, or
other licensing controls.

7. BACKUP AND OPERATIONAL COPIES

The Licensee may make a reasonable number of copies of the Software solely for
